# ==============================================================================
# tools/dx-native-tools/.gitignore
# ==============================================================================
#
# THE FIRST RULE BELOW ("!*") IS LOAD-BEARING - DO NOT DELETE IT.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore is the standard Visual Studio / .NET one. It
# ignores names that also occur in this folder, for example:
#
#     *.env                     -> linux/pins.env
#     *.log  [Oo]ut/  [Ll]og/  [Dd]ebug/  [Rr]elease/ ...
#
# Without the "!*" below, such files would be silently left out of every
# commit, and the build pins would not be there for the next person who cloned
# this repository. A nested .gitignore takes precedence over the ones above it,
# so re-including everything here and then re-ignoring only what this folder
# genuinely produces keeps the root .gitignore untouched. (Same rule, same
# reason, as CodeBrix.WebPlatform.WasmShrink's binaryen-native-tools/.gitignore.)
#
# Verify at any time with:
#     git status --ignored --porcelain -- tools/dx-native-tools
#         -> should list only output/ contents
# ==============================================================================

# Re-include everything under this folder, overriding the root .gitignore.
!*
!*/

# --- what this folder really does produce, and must not commit ---------------

# Built programs, gate runs, logs, the image build context, SHA256SUMS, and
# output/libgit2/ (the libgit2 package and the library taken out of it, which
# must never be committed). ONE tree, shared by every platform build. The
# leading slash matters.
/output/

# cargo's output, if anyone builds a tool in place (the scripts never do: they put the target
# folder outside the source tree). Everything else under sources/ is committed.
/sources/dioxus-cli/target/
/sources/wasm-bindgen-cli/target/
/sources/codebrix-libgit2-sys/target/
/split-check/target/

# Finder droppings (the "!*" above would otherwise re-include them).
.DS_Store
